<!DOCTYPE article PUBLIC "-//NLM//DTD JATS (Z39.96) Journal Archiving and Interchange DTD v1.0 20120330//EN" "JATS-archivearticle1.dtd"><article xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xmlns:mml="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" article-type="research-article"><?properties open_access?><front><journal-meta><journal-id journal-id-type="nlm-ta">J Exp Med</journal-id><journal-id journal-id-type="iso-abbrev">J. Exp. Med</journal-id><journal-id journal-id-type="publisher-id">jexpmed</journal-id><journal-title-group><journal-title>The Journal of Experimental Medicine</journal-title></journal-title-group><issn pub-type="ppub">0022-1007</issn><issn pub-type="epub">1540-9538</issn><publisher><publisher-name>The Rockefeller University Press</publisher-name></publisher></journal-meta><article-meta><article-id pub-id-type="pmid">19870426</article-id><article-id pub-id-type="pmc">2133286</article-id><article-categories><subj-group subj-group-type="heading"><subject>Article</subject></subj-group></article-categories><title-group><article-title>INTERSTITIAL BRONCHOPNEUMONIA </article-title><subtitle>II. PRODUCTION OF INTERSTITIAL MONONUCLEAR PNEUMONIA BY THE BORDET-GENGOU BACILLUS</subtitle></title-group><contrib-group><contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>Sprunt</surname><given-names>Douglas H.</given-names></name></contrib><contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>Martin</surname><given-names>Donald S.</given-names></name></contrib><contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>Williams</surname><given-names>Jarrett E.</given-names></name></contrib></contrib-group><aff id="d33e50">From the Departments of Pathology and Bacteriology of the Duke University School of Medicine, Durham</aff><pub-date pub-type="ppub"><day>31</day><month>8</month><year>1935</year></pub-date><volume>62</volume><issue>3</issue><fpage>449</fpage><lpage>456</lpage><history><date date-type="received"><day>23</day><month>6</month><year>1935</year></date></history><permissions><copyright-statement>Copyright &#x000a9; Copyright, 1935, by The Rockefeller Institute for Medical Research New York</copyright-statement><copyright-year>1935</copyright-year></permissions><abstract><p>Pure cultures of Bordet-Gengou bacilli produce in rabbits an interstitial mononuclear pneumonia which cannot be differentiated from that occurring in children dying of pertussis or from lhat caused in animals by the viruses of epidemic influenza and psittacosis. A similar pneumonia can be produced in rabbits by typhoid bacilli.</p></abstract></article-meta></front></article>